  "id": "theo2",
  "handle": "theo_reads_memos",
  "name": "Theo",
  "bio": "Declassified documents, read so you don't have to.",
  "voice": "am_michael",
  "case": "jfkfiles",
  "look": {
   "skin": "#8a5a3c",
   "hair": "#141014",
   "style": "short",
   "shirt": "#c9b06a",
   "glasses": true,
   "extra": "beard"
  },
  "script": "I spent the spring of 2025 reading JFK files. A law passed in 1992 said every record had to be public by 2017. Presidents kept delaying. Then in March 2025, tens of thousands of pages dropped, most of the black ink gone. What's in them? CIA operations, informants, Oswald's trip to Mexico City. What isn't in them? Proof of a second shooter. Don't take my word for it. Read them yourself. That's the point."
 },
